course: dictionary
lesson: 15445
title: Steepness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Steepness tells you how steep something is. It is how sharply a hill, road, slope or roof goes up or down. «The steepness of the hill made the climb very hard.» The words «very hard» are a clue: a steep hill is tough to climb.
explain: You can see steepness in maps and pictures too. On a map, contour lines show the shape of the land, and when they are close together, the slope is steep. «The steepness of the ramp made the toy car roll faster.» In science, a steeper ramp makes the car go faster.
explain: In maths, steepness describes a line. A steeper line on a graph shows that something is changing faster. The steepness of a line is also called its gradient, or how far it goes up for every step across.
fact: Steepness means how sharply something goes up or down.
fact: «The steepness of the slope» means how steep the slope is.
fact: On a map, contour lines close together show steepness.
fact: In science, a steeper ramp can make a toy car roll faster.
fact: In maths, the steepness of a line is its gradient.
exercise: «The steepness of the hill made the climb very hard.» What does steepness mean here? | How green the hill is | How many people climbed it | How far away the hill is | *How sharply the hill goes up
exercise: In maths, the steepness of a line is measured by its gradient. What is that? | The colour of the line | The number of points on the line | The length of the line | *How far it goes up for each step across
exercise: Which word means how steep a slope is? | roll | ramp | *steepness | toy
test: On a map, what shows the steepness of a hill? | Blue water lines | Pictures of trees | *Contour lines that are close together | Contour lines that are far apart
test: «The steepness of the ramp made the toy car roll faster.» In this science example, what does the steepness change? | The colour of the car | How heavy the car is | *How fast the toy car rolls | The number of wheels
exam: Which phrase means the same as the steepness of a slope? | How smooth the slope feels | How long the slope is | *How sharply the slope goes up or down | How wide the slope is
